cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use RynnValue in your research, please cite it
  using the metadata from this file.
type: software
title: "RynnValue: Scaling Robotic Value Foundation Models with Temporal Distance"
abstract: >-
  RynnValue is a RynnBrain-based vision-language value model
  that predicts, for every frame of a robot manipulation
  video, the minimum remaining time in seconds until the
  task instruction is completed, together with a
  natural-language analysis (video description,
  instruction-video match, and task success verdicts). The
  model uses distributional value heads with two-hot target
  encodings, paired absolute and relative value heads, and a
  prediction-slot-isolated attention scheme. The repository
  also provides an inference toolkit, a reward-model
  evaluation suite built on Robometer (reward alignment,
  policy ranking, confusion matrix), and value-driven
  reinforcement learning of vision-language-action policies
  (offline IQL and online SAC latent steering) built on
  openpi.
authors:
  - name: "RynnValue Team, Alibaba"
keywords:
  - value model
  - reward model
  - robot manipulation
  - vision-language-action
  - vision-language model
  - reinforcement learning
  - embodied AI
  - RynnBrain
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-26"
